<title>NIGERIA: W.African police chiefs meet in Nigeria on crime.</title>
<headline>W.African police chiefs meet in Nigeria on crime.</headline>
<dateline>ABUJA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Police chiefs from eight West African countries on Thursday began a three-day meeting in the Nigerian capital Abuja to find ways to combat crime.</p>
<p>&quot;We should put aside colonial differences to forge a regional cooperative strategy to combat crime in our region,&quot; military ruler General Sani Abacha told the opening session.</p>
<p>Nigeria, Benin, Burkina Faso, Ivory Coast, Gambia, Guinea, Cape Verde and Ghana are attending the meeting, which was convened by the Interpol regional committee for West Africa.</p>
<p>Officials said the police brass would discuss conducting joint patrol operations in the region to stem armed robbery.</p>
</text>
